# The undead wave challenge under the Remnants camp (GlobalObserverBhvr_WavesSpawning "Waves_Underground_Challenge"),
# fought by both players at once: every sleeper stands up on BOTH machines when its wave comes (the client sees what the
# host fights), kills count on both, and the fight ends with FinishedFight on both. Both machines run the observer.
# 35 authored LazyActors in five groups; guids from the live Scene_Actors bundle. Hero 5 slot 0, gvars UndergroundChallenge.
# `ai` answers "lazy" for an unbuilt body. The host asserts active=1; a client's copies are host-driven with their AI off, so it asserts `steered`.

include session.coop
A invincible on
B invincible on
A expect gvar UndergroundChallenge StartFight == 0 timeout=5
A expect gvar UndergroundChallenge FinishedFight == 0 timeout=5

# Between the helmet table and the arena (positions summed from the bundle; check with `state` if a tp lands in rock).
A tp 51700,51400
B tp 51760,51400
A expect creatures Draugr 1500 >= 3 timeout=60
B expect creatures Draugr 1500 >= 3 timeout=60

# What taking the helmet and walking in does: the first wave stands up at once.
A setgvar UndergroundChallenge StartFight 1
B expect gvar UndergroundChallenge StartFight == 1 timeout=15


# ---- Wave01: 3 sleepers, killed by A. ----
# Wave1_Draugr_Spear_06
A expect ai 64cfc9ed-17f2-41be-b034-85afacf3d605 contains active=1 timeout=60
A expect ai 64cfc9ed-17f2-41be-b034-85afacf3d605 !contains mode=KnockOut timeout=60
B expect steered 64cfc9ed-17f2-41be-b034-85afacf3d605 == 1 timeout=20
B expect ai 64cfc9ed-17f2-41be-b034-85afacf3d605 !contains mode=KnockOut timeout=20
A kill 64cfc9ed-17f2-41be-b034-85afacf3d605
